                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lémurs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c86c4fa3-82d1-373a-8635-0e0ca1f4c7ae",
                        "entry_id": "a7062625-367f-3a91-bfd1-1f4c81e0e8bb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom de plusieurs espèces de primates souvent également nommés makis, exclusivement malgaches hormis deux espèces introduites aux Comores."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e5a8f83-7215-4112-9e78-85349825c8e9",
                                "sense_id": "c86c4fa3-82d1-373a-8635-0e0ca1f4c7ae",
                                "text": "Le Lémur à crinière (Varecia variegata), ou Maki vari, ou Lémur vari, est une espèce menacée dans son pays d’origine, Madagascar, à cause de la déforestation et de la chasse."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28b15213-2fcd-44ec-b56a-11c15706d964",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7062625-367f-3a91-bfd1-1f4c81e0e8bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "c86c4fa3-82d1-373a-8635-0e0ca1f4c7ae",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lemur",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lemur",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba4512fd-0fc3-3fc4-9884-8e2d2ef45a5a",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1b037d-1b2d-320c-9a72-b3d60f133239",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Primat aus der Unterordnung der Feuchtnasenaffen, der ausschließlich auf Madagaskar heimisch ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8141f01e-5217-4faa-921b-d4c860510de5",
                                                "sense_id": "ba4512fd-0fc3-3fc4-9884-8e2d2ef45a5a",
                                                "text": "Lemuren sind vom Aussterben bedroht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a19d882-ce68-4376-9545-1db7543ce23a",
                                                "sense_id": "ba4512fd-0fc3-3fc4-9884-8e2d2ef45a5a",
                                                "text": "„Die neuere Systematik teilt die Primaten in vier Unterordnungen: Lemuroidea oder Lemuren, Galagoidea oder Buschbabys und Loris, Tarsioidea oder Gespenstmakis und Simiae oder Affen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a52f0417-afc8-3d3d-a049-93c5fc4b3a0b",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1b037d-1b2d-320c-9a72-b3d60f133239",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Geist einer verstorbenen Person"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dfa3286-fe73-46ee-a669-a9d376ac57fb",
                                                "sense_id": "a52f0417-afc8-3d3d-a049-93c5fc4b3a0b",
                                                "text": "Zu Ehren der Lemuren feierten die Römer das Fest Lemuria."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42085632-f25f-4e6e-a718-7d9a2368e87b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7062625-367f-3a91-bfd1-1f4c81e0e8bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "c86c4fa3-82d1-373a-8635-0e0ca1f4c7ae",
                        "target_lang_word": "lemur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lemur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d1c49a8-ce5f-3828-8380-d758ca8781f8",
                                        "entry_id": "bb8e88a1-0e43-3ac1-ae35-29f8f41ebc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any strepsirrhine primate of the superfamily Lemuroidea, native only to Madagascar and some surrounding islands."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c20c04eb-b5a6-4d49-aa03-b1dc2b67cb06",
                                                "sense_id": "8d1c49a8-ce5f-3828-8380-d758ca8781f8",
                                                "text": "\"Lemurs are naturally very social,\" said Mukobi. \"Wild lemurs live in big family groups, and different species do really well together. Plus, the new lemur habitat is quite large, so each family group can have their own space when they choose to.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b58d2182-aba8-46c2-a7dc-d6e3d8c83771",
                                                "sense_id": "8d1c49a8-ce5f-3828-8380-d758ca8781f8",
                                                "text": "Tucker-Brown explained how lemurs—like much of the “stranded” flora and fauna of Madagascar—are effectively living fossils. Belonging to a primate group called prosimians, lemurs were evolutionarily superseded by monkeys on mainland Africa 35mn years ago and driven to near-extinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2be9731f-a3e4-3b03-8dd1-4618702d301b",
                                        "entry_id": "bb8e88a1-0e43-3ac1-ae35-29f8f41ebc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the genus Lemur, represented by the ring-tailed lemur (Lemur catta)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9dbef0a0-2acb-3456-826d-cfb92f7f4f9b",
                                        "entry_id": "bb8e88a1-0e43-3ac1-ae35-29f8f41ebc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A loris (Lemur tardigradus, now Loris tardigradus), predating the 10th edition of Systema Naturæ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
